%U A400532 1,1,5,1,7,8,9,5,11,1,1,0,3,0,5,0,0,0,9,0,11,0,1
%N A400532 Square array read by downward antidiagonals: T(n,k) is the conductor of chi_{n,k}, where chi_{n,k} is the Dirichlet character modulo n with label k in the Conrey labeling system; T(n,k) = 0 if n and k are not coprime.
%C A400532 Row n is periodic with period n, and the number of occurrences of d in a period is A007431(d) for each divisor d of n.
%H A400532 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400532/b400532.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..11325</a> (first 150 antidiagonals)
%H A400532 LMFDB, <a href="https://www.lmfdb.org/Character/Dirichlet/Labels">Dirichlet character labels</a>.
%F A400532 Each column is multiplicative: T(p^e,k) = 0 if p divides k; for odd prime p, T(p^e,k) = 1 if k == 1 (mod p^e) and p*gcd(ord(k,p^e), p^(e-1)) otherwise; T(2,1) = 1; T(2^e,k) = 1 if k == 1 (mod 2^e), 4 if k == -1 (mod 2^e), and 4*ord(k,2^e) otherwise for e >= 2.
%F A400532 In particular, T(n,k) = n if and only if gcd(n,k) > 1; k !== 1 (mod p) for every prime factor p of n such that p^2 does not divide k; k == 3, 5 (mod 8) if n is divisible by 4; and k^(p-1) !== 1 (mod p^2) for every odd prime p such that p^2 divides k.
